    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cervārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to deer</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lupus,</span>”
				<i>a lynx</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 22, 34, § 84</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 37, 79,
				§ 202</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venenum,</span>”
				<i>an herb with which arrows were smeared</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 11, 76, § 101</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fest. s. v. toxicum, p. 355: cervaria ovis,
					quae pro cervā immolabatur (Dianae),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 57</span></i>
			.</div>
